entor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, TOSHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMAI, KATSUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANO, MINORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for assaying phosphorylation (or dephosphorylation) enzyme activity on a substrate peptide by evaluating the phosphorylation of the substrate peptide which can be phosphorylated by DNA-dependent protein kinase (DNA-PK), ATM and ATR by an immunological technique with the use of an antibody capable of recognizing the phosphorylated state.  Application of this assay method makes it possible to screen compounds controlling these enzyme activities.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une méthode permettant de mesurer une activité enzymatique de phosphorylation (ou de déphosphorylation) sur un peptide substrat, cette méthode consistant notamment à évaluer la phosphorylation de ce peptide substrat, lequel est apte à être phosphorylé par une protéine kinase dépendante de l'ADN (ADN-PK), ATM et ATR, selon une technique immunologique faisant intervenir un anticorps capable de reconnaître un état phosphorylé. L'application de cette méthode de mesure permet de cribler des composés qui régulent ces activités enzymatiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts